- op: discuss  # 1856
  at: '2026-09-26T16:53:58Z'  # 1856
  by: agent  # 1856
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1856
  clock: 3  # 1856
  nonce: '1856'  # 1856
  message: "GO HALF FIXED by PR #1224 (INV-tanom's emitter fix, the direction this item named second). Measured with the production functions: alertmanager's caveat now reads 1,141 of 3,557 method call site(s) (32.1%), was 1,141 of 6,183 (18.5%); gocryptfs 284 of 1,779 (16.0%), was 284 of 3,345 (8.5%). No verdict, caveat kind or evidence count moved on either (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/tanom_fix_09262026/). The unknown_receiver_scope docstring no longer claims commensurability \"by construction\"; it says the denominator is only as good as the producers' stamp.\n\nSTAYS OPEN FOR THE JAVA HALF, and the reason it was not done in the same change: java.yaml declares its qualified statics METHOD-kind (the ADR-0059 shrink-only ledger, WI-ziviv). Restamping Files.readAllBytes as call_construct=function before those rows are function-kind would make method_starved_modules see a function-construct call into a method-only module and report starvation, i.e. WITHHOLD verdicts. So the order is: java.yaml statics to function-kind (WI-ziviv), then the java emitter stamp, then re-measure a Java repo's denominator. No Java repo has been measured for this item yet."  # 1856
